IMPORT prelude

-- Parliamentary Elections Act 1954 (Singapore) -- who may be on the register of electors (ss 5, 6), the candidate's deposit
-- and its forfeiture (s 28), compulsory voting and restoration to the register (s 43), the punishment and incapacities for
-- corrupt and illegal practices (ss 61, 79), the cap on election expenses (s 69, Third Schedule), the employer's duty on
-- polling day (s 76), and the polling-time publication and campaigning bans (ss 61C, 61D, 78C, 78D, 78E, 80).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PEA1954.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 28/3/2025"; the latest amendment seen annotated is S 200/2025
-- (wef 28/03/2025, the Third Schedule); the latest Act annotated is Act 34 of 2024 (wef 22/01/2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a voter, candidate,
-- employer or publisher actually meets. Not encoded: electoral divisions and GRCs, registration procedure and claims and
-- objections, nomination procedure, the conduct of the poll and the count, DRE voting, overseas and postal voting, the
-- definitions of treating, undue influence and bribery (ss 58-60), the election advertising rules beyond the cooling-off ban
-- (ss 61B, 61E-61S), election agents and returns (ss 62-75A), election petitions (Part 4), and the Fourth Schedule Rules.
-- The deposit amount itself (s 28(1AA): an MP's monthly allowance rounded to the nearest $500) is not computed.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parliamentary Elections Act 1954 -- elections`

§§ `5, 6 -- who may be on the register of electors`

-- s 5(1): a person who on the prescribed date "(a) is a citizen of Singapore; (b) is ordinarily resident in Singapore; and
-- (c) is not less than 21 years of age" is entitled to be on the register. (1A): a person is DEEMED ordinarily resident "if
-- the person keeps and maintains a contact address, even though the person is not resident in Singapore on that date".
-- (4): the prescribed date is 1 July unless the Minister orders otherwise.
-- s 6(1): no person is entitled to be on the register if he or she (a) acquired or applied to acquire foreign citizenship by a
-- voluntary act "(other than marriage)", voluntarily exercised rights exclusive to foreign citizens, swore foreign allegiance,
-- or applied for or used a foreign passport; (b) is serving a sentence of imprisonment "for an offence punishable with
-- imprisonment for a term exceeding 12 months"; (c) is found to be of unsound mind; (d) is incapable by reason of a corrupt or
-- illegal practice conviction; (g) has been expunged under s 43(5) and not restored. (1A): a person DEEMED resident is also
-- disqualified if "(a) serving a sentence of imprisonment ... in any prison ... outside Singapore".
-- (2): a foreign conviction does not disqualify under (1)(b) "unless the offence is also one which, had it been committed in
-- Singapore, would have been punishable". (3): voting in a foreign national, state, provincial or metropolitan election "is
-- deemed to be the voluntary claim and exercise of a right" under (1)(a)(ii).
DECLARE Person HAS
    `citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `keeps a contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age on the prescribed date` IS A NUMBER
    `acquired or applied for foreign citizenship other than by marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voted in a foreign national election` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied for or used a foreign passport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `serving a prison sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum term for the offence in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the conviction was outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence would be punishable in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `serving the sentence in a prison outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `found to be of unsound mind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of a corrupt practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of an illegal practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since that conviction` IS A NUMBER
    `expunged for not voting and not restored` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person qualifies under section 5` IF
        `the person`'s `citizen of Singapore`
    AND (`the person`'s `ordinarily resident in Singapore` OR `the person`'s `keeps a contact address`)
    AND `the person`'s `age on the prescribed date` AT LEAST 21

-- INFERENCE: "deemed" resident is read as relying on s 5(1A) -- not actually resident, but keeping a contact address.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is deemed resident` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `ordinarily resident in Singapore`)
    AND `the person`'s `keeps a contact address`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the imprisonment disqualification applies` IF
        `the person`'s `serving a prison sentence`
    AND `the person`'s `maximum term for the offence in months` GREATER THAN 12
    AND ((NOT `the person`'s `the conviction was outside Singapore`) OR `the person`'s `the offence would be punishable in Singapore`)

-- s 61(2): a corrupt practice conviction brings incapacity "for a period of 7 years from the date of his or her conviction of
-- being registered as an elector or of voting"; s 79(1): an illegal practice, 3 years.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is incapable by reason of an election conviction` IF
        (`the person`'s `convicted of a corrupt practice` AND `the person`'s `years since that conviction` LESS THAN 7)
    OR  (`the person`'s `convicted of an illegal practice` AND `the person`'s `years since that conviction` LESS THAN 3)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified under section 6` IF
        `the person`'s `acquired or applied for foreign citizenship other than by marriage`
    OR  `the person`'s `voted in a foreign national election`
    OR  `the person`'s `applied for or used a foreign passport`
    OR  `the imprisonment disqualification applies` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `found to be of unsound mind`
    OR  `the person is incapable by reason of an election conviction` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `expunged for not voting and not restored`
    OR  (`the person is deemed resident` `the person` AND `the person`'s `serving the sentence in a prison outside Singapore`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is entitled to be on the register` IF
        `the person qualifies under section 5` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is disqualified under section 6` `the person`)

§§ `28 -- the candidate's deposit`

-- s 28(1A): without the deposit by 12 noon on nomination day the candidate "is deemed to have withdrawn". (4): the deposit is
-- returned after the result is gazetted, subject to (4A): if the candidate "is not elected and (a) the number of votes polled by
-- the candidate does not exceed one-eighth of the total number of votes polled" -- or, in a GRC, the votes polled by the
-- group -- "the sum deposited is forfeited". (6)(a): votes polled means votes counted other than rejected votes.
GIVEN `elected` IS A BOOLEAN, `votes polled by the candidate or group` IS A NUMBER, `total votes polled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposit is forfeited` IF
        (NOT `elected`)
    AND `votes polled by the candidate or group` TIMES 8 AT MOST `total votes polled`

§§ `43 -- compulsory voting`

-- s 43(1): "Every elector must record his or her vote at each election". (1A), (1B): an elector who votes at a special polling
-- station, or an overseas postal voter who applies for postal voting papers, "must be treated ... as having recorded his or her
-- vote". (5): the names of non-voters are "expunged from the register". (8): restored "without penalty" on a "good and
-- sufficient reason"; (8A): otherwise restored "on payment of the sum of $50".
GIVEN `recorded a vote` IS A BOOLEAN, `treated as having voted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name is expunged under section 43` IF
    (NOT `recorded a vote`) AND (NOT `treated as having voted`)

GIVEN `good and sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the restoration fee` MEANS
    IF `good and sufficient reason` THEN 0 ELSE 50

§§ `61, 79 -- corrupt and illegal practices`

-- s 61(1): personation (or abetting it), treating, undue influence or bribery: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding 3 years or ... both". (d) a knowingly false statement of fact about a candidate's personal character
-- or conduct, (e) a knowingly false statement of another candidate's withdrawal: "a fine or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 12 months" -- NO CAP on the fine is stated. (ea) a false s 73A declaration, (f) a false election expenses
-- declaration: "$2,000 or ... 6 months". (3): no prosecution for a corrupt practice "(except ... (1)(d) and (e))" without the
-- consent of the Public Prosecutor.
DECLARE CorruptPractice IS ONE OF
    `personation`
    `treating`
    `undue influence`
    `bribery`
    `a knowingly false statement about a candidate's character`
    `a knowingly false statement that a candidate has withdrawn`
    `a false post-election declaration under section 73A`
    `a false election expenses declaration`

GIVEN `the practice` IS A CorruptPractice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practice is a false statement offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the practice`
    WHEN `a knowingly false statement about a candidate's character` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a knowingly false statement that a candidate has withdrawn` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the practice` IS A CorruptPractice
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the practice`
    WHEN `a false post-election declaration under section 73A` THEN 6
    WHEN `a false election expenses declaration` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the practice is a false statement offence` `the practice` THEN 12 ELSE 36

GIVEN `the practice` IS A CorruptPractice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is uncapped` IF
    `the practice is a false statement offence` `the practice`

GIVEN `the practice` IS A CorruptPractice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor's consent is needed` IF
    NOT `the practice is a false statement offence` `the practice`

-- s 61(2) and s 79(1): 7 years' incapacity for a corrupt practice; for an illegal practice "a fine not exceeding $2,000" and 3
-- years' incapacity. Either way an elected Member's election "shall be vacated from the date of the conviction".
DECLARE Conviction IS ONE OF
    `a corrupt practice`
    `an illegal practice`

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A Conviction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years of incapacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conviction`
    WHEN `a corrupt practice` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 3

§§ `69 and Third Schedule -- the cap on election expenses`

-- s 69(1): no sum is to be paid or expense incurred by a candidate or election agent "in excess of the amount determined in
-- accordance with the Third Schedule". (1A): that amount "does not include any expenditure incurred by the candidate for his or
-- her personal expenses, or any fee paid to the election agent not exceeding $500". (2): knowingly contravening is an illegal
-- practice. Third Schedule (S 200/2025): "$5 for each elector on the register", and in a GRC that figure "divided by the
-- number of candidates in each group".
GIVEN `electors on the register` IS A NUMBER, `candidates in the group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the expenses cap` MEANS
    5 TIMES `electors on the register` DIVIDED BY `candidates in the group`

-- READING: a fee "not exceeding $500" is excluded; a larger fee is read as NOT excluded at all (rather than only its excess).
GIVEN `election expenses other than personal expenses` IS A NUMBER, `election agent's fee` IS A NUMBER, `electors` IS A NUMBER, `group size` IS A NUMBER, `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expenses are an illegal practice` IF
        `knowingly`
    AND `election expenses other than personal expenses` PLUS `the counted agent fee` `election agent's fee` GREATER THAN `the expenses cap` `electors` `group size`

GIVEN `fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counted agent fee` MEANS
    IF `fee` AT MOST 500 THEN 0 ELSE `fee`

§§ `76 -- employers on polling day`

-- s 76(1): every employer must "allow every elector who is an employee thereof a reasonable period for voting". (1A): no
-- deduction from pay and no penalty for the absence. (2): Railway employees "actually engaged in the running of trains and to
-- whom such time cannot be allowed without interfering with the manning of the trains" are excepted. (3): the OFFENCE is
-- refusing, or interfering by intimidation, undue influence or otherwise, with the reasonable period -- $1,000 or 6 months.
-- The offence in (3) does not mention the deduction forbidden by (1A).
GIVEN `refused or interfered with a reasonable period for voting` IS A BOOLEAN, `deducted pay for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN, `a train crew member who cannot be spared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer contravenes section 76` IF
        (NOT `a train crew member who cannot be spared`)
    AND (`refused or interfered with a reasonable period for voting` OR `deducted pay for the absence`)

GIVEN `refused or interfered with a reasonable period for voting` IS A BOOLEAN, `deducted pay for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN, `a train crew member who cannot be spared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer commits the section 76(3) offence` IF
        (NOT `a train crew member who cannot be spared`)
    AND `refused or interfered with a reasonable period for voting`

§§ `61C, 61D, 78C, 78D, 78E, 80 -- publishing and campaigning around polling day`

-- Days are counted relative to polling day: 0 is polling day, -1 its eve, the writ day a larger negative number.
--
-- s 78C(1): no publishing election survey results "during the period beginning with the day the writ of election is issued ...
-- and ending with the close of all polling stations on polling day" -- $1,500 or 12 months. s 78D(1): no exit-poll statements or
-- forecasts "on polling day before the close of all polling stations" -- $1,500 or 12 months.
GIVEN `the writ day` IS A NUMBER, `the publication day` IS A NUMBER, `before the close of polling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the survey publication falls in the blackout` IF
        `the publication day` AT LEAST `the writ day`
    AND (`the publication day` LESS THAN 0 OR (`the publication day` EQUALS 0 AND `before the close of polling`))

GIVEN `the publication day` IS A NUMBER, `before the close of polling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exit poll publication is banned` IF
    `the publication day` EQUALS 0 AND `before the close of polling`

-- s 78E(1): a defence to prove "(a) that the contravention ... arose from circumstances beyond the person's control; and (b) that
-- the person took all reasonable steps, and exercised all due diligence". The burden is on the person charged ("to prove").
GIVEN `contravened` IS A BOOLEAN, `beyond the person's control` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 78C or 78D offence is made out` IF
    `contravened` AND (NOT (`beyond the person's control` AND `took all reasonable steps`))

-- s 61C(4): the cooling-off period runs from "the eve of polling day" to "the close of polling on polling day". (1) publishing,
-- or (2) publicly displaying, election advertising during it, knowing or where one "ought reasonably to have known" it is
-- election advertising -- $1,000 or 12 months. s 61D exceptions: (1)(a) permissible electoral matter on clothing, lapel pins,
-- badges and the like; (2)(a) private or domestic electronic communication between individuals and (2)(c) news by an
-- authorised news agency (both only against s 61C(1)); (3)(a) non-online advertising lawfully displayed before the cooling-off
-- period and not relocated, altered or modified (only against s 61C(2)).
DECLARE Advertising IS ONE OF
    `a party's online post`
    `a new poster`
    `a T-shirt with permissible electoral matter`
    `a private message between individuals`
    `news by an authorised news agency`
    `a poster lawfully put up earlier and not altered`

GIVEN `the advertising` IS AN Advertising
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 61D exception applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the advertising`
    WHEN `a party's online post` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a new poster` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `before the close of polling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is in the cooling-off period` IF
        `the day` EQUALS -1
    OR  (`the day` EQUALS 0 AND `before the close of polling`)

GIVEN `the advertising` IS AN Advertising, `the day` IS A NUMBER, `before the close of polling` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cooling-off ban is contravened` IF
        `the day is in the cooling-off period` `the day` `before the close of polling`
    AND `knew or ought to have known`
    AND (NOT `a section 61D exception applies` `the advertising`)

-- s 80(1): "on polling day and the eve of polling day" no one may "endeavour to persuade any person to give or dissuade any
-- person from giving his or her vote" or "visit an elector at his or her home or place of work for any purpose in connection
-- with the election" -- $1,500 or 12 months. Unlike the cooling-off period, this runs the whole of polling day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `persuading or dissuading a voter` IS A BOOLEAN, `visiting an elector at home or work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the canvassing ban is contravened` IF
        (`the day` EQUALS -1 OR `the day` EQUALS 0)
    AND (`persuading or dissuading a voter` OR `visiting an elector at home or work`)
